{"id": "EUVD-2026-82169", "enisaUuid": "f971fe8a-a1d0-3b92-830b-53a1fdca81e6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm: Fix task_struct reference leak in recover_worker\n\nget_pid_task() increments the task reference count, but the\ncorresponding put_task_struct() was missing in the else branch,\nleaking a reference on every GPU hang recovery.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/730662/", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c472fde2c8096e16bb46b0605adda2488f300c0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d684f756d029d81db1cd64cd9645556e53fcc784", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40b793714ad8f393ab3d469f9d00b20ebda46257"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93059", "GHSA-785w-94x7-r876"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "21d669d7-0be2-3537-a1f5-513f9c10aa10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "239d41f0-58bf-330d-8334-a10791e8a6ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "2da331d1-66ee-3798-9df3-72ab19d5d727", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "25654a1756a4ace072404e89882d7ba8391900bd <40b793714ad8f393ab3d469f9d00b20ebda46257"}, {"id": "bf8207e6-2c17-37db-9237-2fd904f84530", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "25654a1756a4ace072404e89882d7ba8391900bd <d684f756d029d81db1cd64cd9645556e53fcc784"}, {"id": "cfabaa6f-80ed-371c-a490-0cadb94a4e58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "25654a1756a4ace072404e89882d7ba8391900bd <6c472fde2c8096e16bb46b0605adda2488f300c0"}, {"id": "d9156255-0348-3813-88ad-f2f3e09e45a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "f7a7995d-c35a-3c84-939d